---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';import Photo from '../components/Photo.astro';import References from '../components/References.astro';import ArrowLink from '../components/ArrowLink.astro';
---
<Base title="A changing landscape" description="Reading water, forests and settlement through dated environmental research in the Swat catchment." section="environment" image="bahrain-river">
<section class="environment-hero"><header class="page-heading"><span class="eyebrow">Water · Land · Change</span><h1>The river is<br/>still writing.</h1><p class="deck">A river carries water, sediment and the consequences of what happens along its banks. To look at Swat is also to look at change.</p></header><div class="photo-band"><Photo id="bahrain-river" eager sizes="100vw"/></div></section>
<div class="reading-layout"><aside class="reading-aside"><span class="eyebrow">Read a connected landscape</span><nav class="chapter-links"><a href="#connections">A catchment in relation</a><a href="#floods">The 2022 floods</a><a href="#forest">Forests & renewal</a><a href="#lake">Traces in a lake</a></nav></aside><article class="reading-copy"><section id="connections"><h2>Upstream is<br/>never far away.</h2><p>The tributary valleys around Kalam meet the main river corridor. Slopes, streams and settlements form connected parts of a catchment. What moves through one part can affect another.</p><div class="catchment" data-view="water"><span class="eyebrow">Read the relationships</span><div class="catchment-tabs" aria-label="Catchment perspective"><button data-view="water" aria-pressed="true">Water</button><button data-view="land" aria-pressed="false">Land</button><button data-view="settlement" aria-pressed="false">Settlement</button></div><svg viewBox="0 0 640 230" role="img" aria-label="Conceptual valley cross section: slopes drain toward a river between settled areas"><path class="diagram-land" d="M0 45L70 20 150 120 230 165 275 180M365 180L430 160 510 80 580 40 640 70"/><path class="diagram-corridor" d="M220 165L420 165 460 210 180 210Z"/><path class="diagram-water" d="M290 170Q310 185 330 170L355 210H265Z"/><g class="diagram-buildings" fill="#788c6c"><path d="M225 165v-25h20v25ZM380 165v-32h25v32ZM410 160v-22h18v22Z"/></g><g fill="#eeeae1" font-family="Arial" font-size="13"><text x="50" y="110">Slopes</text><text x="280" y="230">River</text><text x="425" y="190">Settlement</text></g></svg><p class="diagram-panel" aria-live="polite">Water joins the slopes to the channel. Tributaries collect flow from different branches of the catchment before those waters meet downstream.</p><p class="caption">Conceptual cross section · Not a map, flood simulation or measured terrain profile.</p></div></section><section id="floods"><h2>After the water rose.</h2><p>The 2022 monsoon floods altered parts of the Swat river corridor. A 2025 study combines field observations, satellite analysis and numerical modelling to examine the interaction of flooding, sediment and geological hazards.</p><div class="event-line"><span>2022</span><p>Flooding exposed the close relationship between river processes and development beside the channel. Erosion, sediment movement and debris can change how water passes through a valley.</p></div><div class="event-line"><span>2025</span><p>Researchers published their analysis of the 2022 event. Simulations explore possible processes; they should not be confused with measurements of every location or predictions for an individual building.</p></div><p>This experience does not reconstruct the flood from scenic photographs. The photographs retain their actual capture dates, and the research remains linked for its methods and limits.</p><References ids={['flood']}/></section><section id="forest"><h2>A forest is<br/>also its future.</h2><p>Research published in 2015 examined thirteen forest stands around Malam Jabba. It considered stand structure and regeneration, including younger growth that helps reveal whether a forest is renewing itself.</p><p>The presence of mature trees alone cannot answer that question. The findings belong to the sampled stands and their survey period; they do not establish the present condition of every forest in Swat.</p><References ids={['forest']}/><ArrowLink href="/places/malam-jabba/" label="Read the Malam Jabba note"/></section><section id="lake"><h2>What the view<br/>does not show.</h2><p>At Mahodand, a study published in 2023 detected microplastics in water and in the digestive tracts of sampled brown trout. Samples were collected during summer 2019.</p><p>The finding adds another scale to the landscape: traces too small to see in a panoramic photograph. The study is a dated investigation, not a live water-quality reading.</p><References ids={['lakeStudy']}/><ArrowLink href="/places/mahodand/" label="Return to Mahodand"/></section></article></div>
<div class="photo-band captioned"><Photo id="ushu-forest" caption sizes="100vw"/></div><section class="environment-tease"><div><span class="eyebrow">Keep the whole valley in view</span><h2>Follow the connections.</h2><p>Return to the atlas to locate the places behind these studies.</p></div><ArrowLink href="/atlas/?lens=memory" label="Open the memory lens"/></section>
<script>const descriptions:Record<string,string>={water:'Water joins the slopes to the channel. Tributaries collect flow from different branches of the catchment before those waters meet downstream.',land:'Vegetation, soil and rock shape how slopes respond to water. Erosion and sediment movement connect the hillsides with the river corridor.',settlement:'Where people build changes their relationship to river processes. The 2022 flood research examines development and hazards along the Swat corridor; this diagram does not map risk.'};document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('.catchment-tabs button').forEach(button=>button.addEventListener('click',()=>{const parent=button.closest<HTMLElement>('.catchment');if(!parent)return;parent.dataset.view=button.dataset.view;parent.querySelectorAll('button').forEach(b=>b.setAttribute('aria-pressed',String(b===button)));const text=parent.querySelector('.diagram-panel');if(text)text.textContent=descriptions[button.dataset.view??'water']??'';}));</script>
</Base>
